    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How it is cooked, how it tastes",
     "texto": [
      "A **balanced** diet includes a variety of foods: **fruta**, **verdura**, **legumbres**, **pescado**… Each person needs different things, and there is no single menu for everyone.\n\nTo say how a dish is cooked:\n\n- **a la plancha**, **frito**, **hervido**, **crudo**\n\nTo say what it tastes like: **salado**, **dulce**, **amargo**, **picante**, **soso** (without salt).\n\nWith **sentar bien / mal** we say how a food affects us: el marisco **me sienta mal**; las legumbres **me sientan bien**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Flavours and «sentar bien»",
     "texto": [
      "**Estar** describes how a dish tastes right now: la sopa **está** sosa. **Ser** gives a general characteristic: el limón **es** ácido.\n\nThe adjective agrees with the food: pescado **frito**, verduras **crudas**, carne **muy hecha**.\n\n**Sentar bien / mal** works like **gustar**: the food is the subject and the verb agrees with it; the person goes in the pronoun.\n\n- El marisco **me sienta** mal.\n- Las legumbres **te sientan** bien."
     ],
